D3D12 backend: draw KZ3's boot screen through its own fragment programs.

Found on KZ3's boot/loading screen (the full-screen "blue quad", checkpoint kz3-first-ui-draws):
1. rsx_fp_decompiler.c declared r[48]/h[48], but FP source/destination register fields are 6 bits; KZ3's
   99-instruction boot-screen program uses h50, failed to compile (E5019) and the draw fell back to the
   built-in colour PS (vertex colour: the solid blue / gradient). Now r[64]/h[64].
2. vp_get_fp_pso passed RSX_FP_CTRL_AUTO, so the decompiler guessed the export file from which of r0/h0 was
   written. KZ3 writes coordinates to r0 and its colour to h0..h8 (half exports); the guess exported r0..r4.
   The draw's SET_SHADER_CONTROL 32-bit-exports bit (already captured as fp_exp32 and in the PSO key) is now
   passed through. FP_CTRL_AUTO=1 restores the guess.
3. Guest textures were uploaded only for B8, A8R8G8B8, G8B8 and DXT1/3/5; every other format bound a null
   SRV (KZ3 samples six 64x1 W16Z16Y16X16_FLOAT tables). Now every format rsx_texture_layout() classifies
   (packed 16-bit colours, HILO, depth, X16, Y16X16, F16/F32) is uploaded, with one DXGI mapping
   (tex_decoded_dxgi) shared by the resource and its SRV.
4. SCREEN_AS_TEX (swap any display-sized texture for the last presented frame) is now opt-in: it turned
   KZ3's own 1280x720 scene target into a feedback loop that saturated the screen to white.
Diagnostics: DRAWLOG=<N> (per replayed draw: pipeline or FALLBACK, target, viewport, blend, textures and
sampler slots), FP_DUMP_MATCH=<text> (dump programs whose HLSL contains text, to fp_match.hlsl), and a
guest-FP PSO failure now prints its key and the debug-layer messages (D3D12_DBG=1; FP_FAIL_DUMP=1 keeps
the HLSL). KZ3 port RSX, 2026-10-07; tested with tools/smoke/host_kz3.c and KZ3 under Proton.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.15.0 (SPU pass 81): context only, upstream buffer size macro taken.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.17.0 (SPU pass 95): partly absorbed: the FP export-width bit is #396 (switch now RSX_FP_CTRL_AUTO).

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): DRAWLOG block after upstream's OMSetStencilRef; its /s<idx> sampler field dropped (2001's samp index gone).

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.19.0 (shared v0.19 group C): upstream #635 added vp_tex_dxgi (the same decoded-format map as tex_decoded_dxgi, which is dropped) and widened the bound formats to B8, A8R8G8B8, G8B8, DXT, W16Z16Y16X16, X16, Y16X16, X32F and Y16X16F; tex_fmt_uploadable keeps the rest (packed 16-bit colours, D8R8G8B8, HILO, depth, W32Z32Y32X32F) and gates both checks. PSO-failure print stays under PS3_LOG_FIRST.

